user Artist is "someone who makes doodles and keeps them in lists" with {
  briefly as "The only kind of person ToDoodles serves"
  described as {
    |An artist draws small pictures and files them under names of their own
    |choosing. ToDoodles has no other roles: there is no administrator and
    |no reviewer.
  }
}

epic MakeAndFileADoodle is {

  user Artist wants to "draw a doodle and file it under a name"
    so that "the drawing can be found again later"

  case StartADoodle is {
    user Artist wants to "start a new doodle"
      so that "there is something to draw on"
    step focus user Artist on group Studio
    step take form StartDoodle from user Artist
    step send command ToDoodles.Doodle.Drawing.CreateDrawing
      from source ToDoodles.ToDoodlesApp.DrawingRequests to sink ToDoodles.Doodle.Intake
  } with {
    briefly as "Starting a doodle from the studio screen"
    described as {
      |The artist names a doodle on the studio screen and the application
      |echoes it back, then turns it into a command for the Doodle context.
      |
      |There is deliberately no `show … to …` step here. That step kind is
      |currently unusable: the parser hardcodes an empty relationship on it
      |(EpicParser.showOutputStep), so every such step fails the "must have a
      |non-empty relationship" check no matter how it is written. Filed
      |against riddl; restore the step once that is fixed.
    }
  }

} with {
  briefly as "How an artist makes a doodle and files it"
  described as {
    |The one story ToDoodles tells: an artist arrives at the studio, names a
    |new doodle, and sees it appear in their gallery. Everything the model
    |defines exists to serve this.
  }
}
